# PC-99: every text file is checked out with LF on every platform, whatever core.autocrlf says.
# The licence files are hashed byte for byte (test/license.test.js), the release fixture is
# signed over its LF bytes (test/openpgp.test.js), and the process tests run the checkout's fake
# tools (test/fake-*.js) through their shebang lines, which a CRLF checkout breaks.
* text=auto eol=lf
